      "math_academy_id": "e-5773",
      "problem": "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=2+7\\textrm{i}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226152/assets/da91da7425e6a02a202881eb1db3f1049d3f9cd204c0c1793c30e2d95676783b.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $0<      \\arg(z)<      \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$ Further,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{7}{2})≈1.29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto two decimal places.",
